You are building a catalog-style landing page inspired by ArtCraft's "Crafting Apps" page (not a clone). The goal is to persuade [AUDIENCE] to download or explore [PRODUCT], a family of related tools. The mode is persuade, with a restrained, engineered, drafting-table feel: warm paper, ink-black type, hairline rules, tiny monospace labels, and colour only in the product icons and one accent word per headline. Use [CONTENT] for all copy and products.

**Tech stack:** Next.js (App Router) + React + Tailwind CSS using the CSS variables below, `next/font` (Archivo variable, Inter, Geist Mono), framer-motion for reveals, Lenis for smooth scroll.

```css
:root{
  --bg:#f2f1ee; --bg-raised:#faf9f7; --bg-sunken:#e9e8e4;
  --ink:#101014; --ink-strong:#000; --muted:#1010149e; --faint:#1010146b;
  --line:#10101429; --line-strong:#10101466;
  --accent:#2d81ff; --accent-ink:#1659c4;
  --invert-bg:#101014; --invert-fg:#f2f1ee; --danger:#b3261e;
  --c-blue:#2f7bf5; --c-red:#e8573f; --c-violet:#8b5cf6; --c-amber:#f2a516; --c-teal:#12a58a;
  --font-display:"Archivo",system-ui,sans-serif;
  --font-body:"Inter",system-ui,sans-serif;
  --font-mono:"Geist Mono",ui-monospace,monospace;
  --fs-h1:60px; --fs-h1-lg:72px; --fs-h3:30px; --fs-h4:24px;
  --fs-lede:18px; --fs-body:16px; --fs-mono:11px; --fs-mono-sm:10px;
  --track-display:-0.035em; --track-mono:0.15em;
  --s1:8px; --s2:16px; --s3:24px; --s4:32px; --s6:48px; --s10:96px;
  --container:1280px; --nav-h:49px; --radius:0px; --radius-icon:20px; --shadow:none;
  --ease-out:cubic-bezier(0,0,.2,1); --ease-std:cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);
}
[data-theme="dark"]{--bg:#101014;--ink:#f2f1ee;--ink-strong:#fff;--line:#f2f1ee29;--invert-bg:#f2f1ee;--invert-fg:#101014}
body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:400 16px/1.5 var(--font-body)}
```

**Page structure**
1. **Sticky nav (49px).** Cells separated by 1px `--line` vertical rules. Logo cell, mono uppercase links, one active link as a solid ink chip. On the right: Pricing, icon cells (community, theme toggle), and a full-height solid ink "LAUNCH APP" cell. A 1px bottom border runs full width.
2. **Hero.** Inside a 1280px frame with 1px side rules and small "+" crop marks at the corners. Top index bar: "01 / [SECTION]" on the left and faint mono meta on the right. Two columns. Left: H1 (Archivo 620, 60px/1.02, -2.1px, two lines, one word in `--accent-ink`), an 18px muted lede, a button row (solid primary plus two outlined secondary), a mono OS caption, a "Recommended:" note with an underlined link, and a segmented SHARE strip. Right: a grid of 13 app icons (5/5/3, 80px, 20px radius, saturated flat colours with engraved-style illustration) with 14px Inter muted captions.
3. **Lineup.** Index bar "02 / THE LINEUP". A 4-column grid with 1px borders. Each cell has: a 24px colored number chip with white mono digits, a right-aligned mono category, a screenshot crop (about 16:10), an icon overlapping the screenshot's lower-left edge, a 24px title (name in ink + a suffix in accent), a one-line grey description, mono 10px bordered status tags, and "EXPLORE NAME ↗". The final cell is a "more on the way" note with a button. Fill leftover cells with `--bg-sunken`.
4. **Principles.** Index bar. H2 with one accent word, then a 3x2 hairline grid. Each cell has a thin line icon, a mono index at top right, a 24px title and 2 lines of grey copy.
5. **CTA.** A centered H2 with accent words, a short muted line and one solid ink button.
6. **Footer.** A logo with tagline plus 4 link columns under mono uppercase headers (faint), 14px links, and a bottom bar with © and a mono slogan.

**Components**
- Button primary: height 48px, padding 0 24px, `--ink` bg, `--bg` text, mono 11px/700 uppercase, 0.15em tracking, radius 0, with a 16px leading icon. Hover: bg lightens to #2a2a30 over 120ms linear.
- Button secondary: same size, transparent bg, 1px `--line-strong` border, ink text. Hover: bg `--bg-sunken`.
- Share strip: a 36px-high segmented control with 1px borders, 8px 12px padding, mono 11px.
- Tags: 1px `--line` border, 10px mono uppercase, padding 2px 6px. Status "ready" is ink, "alpha" is faint.
- Cards are open cells with hairline borders only. No bg, shadow or radius.
- No inputs on this page. If needed, use 1px borders, radius 0, and a mono label above.

**Motion:** Lenis smooth scroll. Sections and cells fade up 12px over 400-500ms with `--ease-out`, staggered 40-60ms. Icon and screenshot hover: scale 1.03 over 300ms `--ease-out`. Colour and opacity transitions run 150ms `--ease-std`. The "↗" arrow nudges 2px. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Optional mono marquee ticker.

**Responsive:** At 1440 the frame is 1280. At 1024 the lineup becomes 3 columns, and at 768 it becomes 2. At 640 and below the grid is 1 column, the hero is single column, the buttons stack full-width-ish at 48px height, and the icon grid wraps to 3 per row. Nav collapses to logo, theme toggle and hamburger. H1 scales to about 40-48px with the same tracking. Keep 16-24px gutters and the 1px frame lines.

**Copy tone:** Terse, confident, technical, honest about status. Examples: "Thirteen apps. One craft." / "Built the hard way." / "Build it with us." Use mono numbered indexes ("01 / THE LINEUP"), and no hype adjectives or exclamation marks.

**Anti-patterns:** No rounded cards, shadows, glassmorphism, gradients, emoji icons, centered-everything layouts, pure white backgrounds, multiple accent colours in the chrome, or a sans-serif for labels. No uniform three-card marketing grids with big icons.

**Final checklist**
- Background is warm #f2f1ee and text is #101014, with no pure white.
- Headlines are Archivo about 60px, tight at -2.1px, with exactly one blue accent word.
- Every label, button and tag is Geist Mono uppercase at 10-11px with wide tracking.
- The page is framed by 1px hairlines with section index bars and crop marks, and there are no shadows and no radii on chrome.
- The sticky 49px nav has hairline-divided cells and a solid ink "Launch" block at the right.
- Colour appears only in the app icons, the number chips and the accent words.
- The lineup is a 4-column hairline grid with screenshot, overlapping icon, title, tags and an "Explore ↗" link.
- Motion is subtle (fade-up reveals, 300ms hover scale, 150ms colour) with Lenis smooth scroll.

You are building a one-page, scroll-driven portfolio for [PRODUCT] (a creative individual or tiny studio), aimed at [AUDIENCE], and inspired by the quiet, cosmic, WebGL-particle language of high-end creative-developer portfolios. This is not a clone. Mode: **experience**. The website is the showcase. A full-viewport monochrome particle "world" carries the emotion, the typography is deliberately small and restrained, and scrolling plays the page like a timeline of cinematic 100vh scenes. Content to present: [CONTENT].

**Tech stack**
Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript, SCSS Modules, `lenis` for smooth scroll, and `three` (optionally `@react-three/fiber`) for the particle system with custom GLSL shaders. Load Inter Tight via `next/font/google`. No Tailwind, no UI kit, no GSAP needed: map Lenis scroll progress to shader uniforms yourself.

**Design tokens**
```css
:root {
  /* color */
  --background: #222124;
  --surface-alt: #27262a;
  --foreground: #f0f2f0;
  --muted: #8b8f8c;
  --accent: #f4ce15;
  --accent-secondary: #379777;
  --hairline: rgba(240, 242, 240, 0.12);

  /* type */
  --font-sans: "Inter Tight", system-ui, -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  --fs-label: 12px;   /* mono, +0.04em */
  --fs-body: 15px;    /* lh 1.4 */
  --fs-voice: 22.5px; /* lh 26.25px — name, role, statements, project titles */
  --fs-statement: 36px; /* max, once per scene, lh 1.15, -0.01em */
  --lh-voice: 1.1667;
  --fw: 400;

  /* spacing (8px base) */
  --s-1: 8px; --s-2: 16px; --s-3: 24px; --s-4: 40px; --s-5: 64px; --s-6: 120px;
  --gutter: clamp(20px, 2.8vw, 40px);
  --scene: 100svh;

  /* shape & light */
  --radius-dot: 50%;
  --glow: 0 0 10px 2px rgb(240, 242, 240);

  /* motion */
  --ease: ease;
  --ease-io: ease-in-out;
  --ease-out-soft: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  --dur-hover: 0.3s;
  --dur-reveal: 0.6s;
  --dur-reveal-slow: 0.7s;
  --dur-loader-out: 1.2s;
}
html, body { background: var(--background); color: var(--foreground); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--fs-body); font-weight: 400; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
```

**Page structure** (stacked full-height sections over one fixed canvas)
- **Fixed layers:** (1) a full-screen WebGL canvas, `position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 0`. It holds a starfield of about 1,500 tiny off-white points (0.5–2px, 20–70% opacity) plus a central "world" of 2–6k soft, blurred particles distributed on a sphere of about 15–20vh radius, rotating slowly on Y, with brighter points toward the camera so it reads as a lit crescent while turning. (2) A grain overlay, `position: fixed; inset: -50%; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.07; z-index: 50`, with animated noise. (3) An optional 8px glowing cursor dot.
- **Loader (overlay, 100svh):** the particle world is centered. One counter label ("0%"–"100%") in `--fs-body` / 15px sits exactly at its center in `--foreground`. Nothing else is on screen. At 100%, fade the overlay out (opacity, 1.2s ease-in-out), then enable scroll.
- **Scene 1, Hero (100svh):** the h1 is [PRODUCT]'s name and a p gives the role. Both are 22.5px / 400 / lh 26.25px, stacked, top-left at the gutter. Optionally add a 12px mono location/availability label with a 6px `--accent-secondary` dot bottom-left, and "Scroll" in muted 12px bottom-right. The particle world stays centered.
- **Scenes 2–4 (100svh each):** one short first-person statement per scene from [CONTENT] (what you do, how, why it is fast or crafted), at 22.5–36px, max-width 18ch–28ch, anchored to a different corner or edge each time. Each scene sets a new target shape for the particles (sphere → ring → scattered field → horizontal band).
- **Scene 5, Services/Approach (about 200svh, sticky inner):** pin a 100svh frame. A short list of 3–5 capabilities is revealed one by one as the user scrolls, at 22.5px with a muted 12px mono index ("01", "02"…).
- **Scene 6, Selected work (about 470svh, sticky inner):** pin the frame. Projects advance with scroll. Show one at a time: the title at 22.5px, a muted 15px line (role, year, client) and a small "View project" link. The particle world reframes behind each project. A project visual, if used, is a single unframed image or video with 0 radius that fades in at reduced size. No card grid.
- **Scene 7, Contact (100svh):** a single invitation line at 22.5–36px, the email as a large-ish text link, socials as a 15px inline list, and a muted 12px sign-off/copyright at the bottom edge. The particles settle back into the opening sphere.
- Alternate scene backgrounds between `--background` and `--surface-alt` only if needed for separation. Never use borders between sections.

**Component specs**
- **Text link:** 15px or 22.5px, `--foreground` (or `--muted` at rest in lists). Add a pseudo-element underline, 1px tall, `width: 0 → 100%` with `transition: width 0.3s ease`, and change the colour to `--foreground` on hover. Use an `--accent` underline for at most one link per page (the email).
- **Nav:** none. If a fixed element is required, use the name (15px) top-left and "Contact" (15px, text link) top-right, both with `mix-blend-mode: difference` and no background bar.
- **Status dot:** 6–8px, `border-radius: 50%`, `background: var(--accent-secondary)` or `--accent`, `box-shadow: 0 0 10px 2px` in the same colour at reduced alpha.
- **Cursor dot:** 8px, `border-radius: 50%`, `background: var(--foreground)`, `box-shadow: var(--glow)`. It follows the pointer with a lerp of about 0.15 and scales to 2.5× over links.
- **Cards and inputs:** none. If a contact form is unavoidable, use underline-only inputs: 1px `--hairline` bottom border, 22.5px text, a `--muted` placeholder and an `--foreground` focus border. No radius and no fill.
- **Focus:** `outline: 1px solid var(--foreground); outline-offset: 4px`.

**Motion spec**
- Lenis: `lerp: 0.08–0.1`, `smoothWheel: true`. Expose `progress` per section to the canvas.
- Particle shaders: soft round sprites (`smoothstep` radial falloff), additive blending, size attenuation and per-point random phase. Morph between target positions with `mix(a, b, uProgress)` per scene, damped (about 0.06 per frame). Rotate the world constantly (about 0.05 rad/s) with slight mouse parallax (±3°).
- Starfield: very slow drift and a parallax shift with scroll (about 0.1× scroll speed).
- Text reveals: opacity 0 → 1 over 0.6s ease (secondary lines 0.7s), triggered once when a scene is about 40% in view. Allow at most an 8px translate. No staggered letter animations or bounces.
- Grain: `@keyframes grain` jumping between 8 translate offsets, `animation: grain 0.8s steps(8) infinite`.
- "World" spin: `@keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg) } }` over about 40s linear, for any decorative ring or SVG.
- Loader out: opacity 1.2s ease-in-out, then remove from the DOM.
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable Lenis smoothing, freeze rotation and grain, keep morphs but jump to targets instantly.

**Responsive rules**
- Every scene is `min-height: 100svh`. Sticky chapters keep their multi-viewport scroll lengths.
- Under 768px: the gutter is 20px, the voice size stays 22.5px, the statement size is capped at 28px and text anchors to the top or bottom of the scene (never over the world's center). The loader stays perfectly centered.
- Halve the particle counts on mobile and on `devicePixelRatio > 2`, and clamp DPR to 1.5. Pause rendering when the tab is hidden.
- There must be no horizontal scroll at any width.

**Copy tone**
First person, calm, confident and short. Name the craft and the outcome, then stop. No exclamation marks, emoji or buzzword strings. Example lines in this voice:
- "I build the parts of the web people remember."
- "Ambitious designs, shipped fast and running smoothly."
- "Motion, performance and the details in between."

**Anti-patterns to avoid**
- Big bold display headlines, gradient text, or a "Hi 👋 I'm…" hero.
- Pure black or white, or colourful or purple-blue nebula particles.
- Card grids, rounded thumbnails, drop shadows, glassmorphism.
- A standard navbar with a pill "Hire me" button.
- Snappy, springy or staggered-letter animations. Everything here is slow fades and drift.
- Accent colours used for fills or large areas.
- Spinners or skeletons in place of the percentage loader.
- Centered blocks of paragraph text. Text sits at edges and corners, and the center belongs to the particles.

**Final checklist**
1. The first paint shows only the charcoal starfield, a centered cluster of soft particles and a small "%" counter that climbs to 100% and fades out over about 1.2s.
2. The background is `#222124` with visible animated film grain, and the text is `#f0f2f0`, not pure white.
3. The name and role are the same size (22.5px / 400, Inter Tight), and nothing on the page is bold or above about 40px.
4. The particle world stays fixed behind the content, visibly rotates and changes shape between scroll chapters.
5. Each section is one viewport tall or a multiple of one, and the work and services chapters are pinned while scrolling.
6. Yellow `#f4ce15` and green `#379777` appear only as tiny signals (dots, one underline), never as fills.
7. There are no cards, borders, rounded corners or nav bar. The only radius is 50% on dots, and the only shadow is the soft glow.
8. Motion feels slow and cinematic (Lenis smoothing, 0.6–1.2s fades, 0.3s hover underlines), and reduced-motion users get a calm static version.

You are building a marketing landing page for [PRODUCT], aimed at [AUDIENCE], inspired by Linear's website (not a clone: do not copy its logo, wording or imagery). Mode: persuade, but in a restrained, product-led way. The page is dark, almost grayscale, typographically precise, and the real product UI is the main visual. The goal is to make [PRODUCT] feel fast, serious and well-made. Use [CONTENT] for the real feature names, copy and mockup data.

**Tech stack:** Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript, CSS Modules or plain CSS using the variables below, Inter Variable via `next/font` (mono: JetBrains Mono or Geist Mono), Radix primitives for menus, Vaul for the mobile drawer, inline SVG icons, and IntersectionObserver for scroll reveals. No Tailwind defaults, no component library look.

**Design tokens:**
```css
:root {
  --bg: #08090a; --bg-2: #090a0b; --bg-3: #101112;
  --surface: #0f1011; --surface-raised: #161718; --surface-3: #1c1c1d;
  --text: #f7f8f8; --text-strong: #d0d6e0; --text-muted: #8a8f98; --text-faint: #62666d;
  --border: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); --border-strong: #2e2e32;
  --pill-bg: #e5e5e6; --pill-text: #08090a;
  --font-sans: "Inter Variable", "SF Pro Display", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  --font-mono: "Berkeley Mono", "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
  --w-light: 300; --w-normal: 400; --w-medium: 510; --w-semibold: 590;
  --fs-h1: 64px; --fs-h2: 48px; --fs-h3: 20px; --fs-h4: 16px; --fs-body: 15px; --fs-ui: 13px; --fs-micro: 12px;
  --ls-h1: -1.408px; --ls-h2: -1.056px; --ls-h3: -0.24px; --ls-body: -0.165px;
  --header-h: 72px; --header-blur: 20px;
  --page-max: 1344px; --outer-pad: 46px; --inset: 32px; --pad-block: 64px;
  --r-4: 4px; --r-6: 6px; --r-8: 8px; --r-12: 12px; --r-16: 16px; --r-pill: 9999px;
  --shadow-ring: 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  --shadow-inset: inset 0 0 12px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  --shadow-float: 0 2px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
  --ease: cubic-bezier(0.25,0.46,0.45,0.94);
  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.32,0.72,0,1);
  --t-quick: .1s; --t-base: .16s; --t-slow: .7s;
}
body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text-muted); font: 400 15px/24px var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: var(--ls-body); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
```

**Page structure (top to bottom):**
1. **Header**: fixed, 72px, 1px bottom border, `backdrop-filter: blur(20px)` over a ~80% #08090a background. Logo mark plus wordmark at left. Links at right: Product, Resources (dropdown triggers), Customers, Pricing, Now, Contact, a 1px vertical divider, "Log in" in muted text, and a "Sign up" light pill.
2. **Hero**: about 200px of top space. Left-aligned two-line h1 (max ~14 words, 64px). Under it, a one-line muted subhead. On the same row, right-aligned, a small announcement: bold white "New" plus muted "[Feature] →".
3. **Hero mockup**: a ~1320px wide, 12px radius, 1px border app window. It has a sidebar (nav items with 14px icons, grouped under tiny muted headings), a main issue/detail view with title, mono inline code chips and an activity feed, and a floating agent/chat panel overlapping the lower right with `--shadow-float`. Use 12–13px text. Put a soft radial gray glow under it and fade the bottom edge into the page.
4. **Logo strip**: 6–7 monochrome wordmarks in one row, evenly spaced. Below it, a 10–11px uppercase mono caption in --text-faint.
5. **Statement**: a 48px/48px paragraph, left-aligned, max ~1000px. The first sentence is --text-muted and the second is --text, or the reverse for emphasis.
6. **Three figures**: three columns separated by 1px vertical hairlines. Each has a mono "FIG 0.1" label, a thin-line isometric SVG (white strokes at ~40%), a 15px/590 title, and a muted 2-line description.
7. **Feature sections ×4** (~1200px tall each): a 12-column grid. At left (cols 1–5) is a 40–48px two-line heading (e.g. "Intake / and integrations"). At right (cols 7–12) is a muted 15px paragraph with a "Learn more →" link. Below is a large UI mockup that bleeds off the right or bottom edge with `mask-image` fades. At the bottom is a "Features" label with a 2–3 column list of arrow links. Each mockup shows a different view (thread to issue, timeline/chart, agent panel, diff/review).
8. **Changelog**: a row of 3–4 cards (surface bg, 1px border, 12px radius), each with a date in mono, a title and a thumbnail.
9. **Closing CTA**: a 48px heading, a Sign up pill and a secondary link. Follow it with a multi-column footer in 13px muted links, on a 1px top border.

**Components:**
- Nav links: 16px, w400, #f7f8f8 (or muted), no underline. Hover transitions color in 0.16s. Header-menu triggers are 32px-high pills with 0 12px padding, 13px text, --text-muted, and on hover a faint white 6% background.
- Primary button (Sign up): height 32px, padding 0 14px, radius 9999px, bg #e5e5e6, text #08090a, 13px/510. Hover: `filter: brightness(1.08)`.
- Ghost button/link: transparent, --text-muted, hover --text, with an optional "→" that shifts 2px right.
- Card/panel: bg --surface, `1px solid var(--border)`, radius 12px, no shadow (except floating panels).
- Chips and tags: 20–22px tall, radius 4–6px, 12px/510 text, 1px border, bg rgba(255,255,255,.04). Inline code: mono 12px, radius 4px, 1px border.
- Avatars 50% radius, 16–20px. Status icons are 14px thin-stroke SVGs. Only status icons get color (yellow, indigo, teal, red).
- Inputs (in mockups): a 13–14px composer with a surface-raised bg, 1px border, radius 8px, and a small indigo send button.

**Motion:** Color/background/filter transitions run 0.1–0.16s with `--ease`. Transform runs 0.15s ease. Scroll reveals use opacity 0 → 1 plus translateY(12px → 0) over 0.5–0.7s with `--ease-out`, triggered once at ~20% in view. Mockup interiors may animate in lightly (rows appearing in sequence, chart dots fading in). The mobile menu and drawer slide or scale in at 0.3–0.7s. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. No bounce, parallax or cursor effects.

**Responsive:** Desktop container is 1344px with 46px outer padding. Below ~1100px the heading/description rows stack and the inset becomes 24px. Below 768px:
- The header shows the logo, Log in, Sign up and a hamburger that opens a full-height drawer.
- The h1 drops to ~40px and wraps to 3–4 lines.
- The statement drops to ~28px.
- The three figures stack.
- Mockups keep their natural size (≥720px wide) and bleed off the right edge, with a fade, instead of scaling down.
- Feature lists go to one column.
- Tap targets are at least 44px.

**Copy tone:** Declarative, short, confident, with no hype words or exclamation marks. Sentence case. Concrete product nouns. Two-part headings with a line break. Example headlines:
- "The [domain] system for teams and agents"
- "Plan, track, / and ship together"
- "Built for the future. Available today."

**Anti-patterns:** no brand accent color on UI chrome, no purple-blue gradients, no glassmorphism cards, no emoji or icon-in-circle feature grids, no centered hero, no pure black or pure white, no heavy shadows, no stock photography, no bold 700 headlines, no colored logos, no bouncy animation.

**Final checklist:**
- [ ] Background is #08090a. Text is only #f7f8f8, #d0d6e0, #8a8f98 and #62666d, and color appears only inside mockups.
- [ ] The h1 is 64px, weight 510, tracking about -1.4px, left-aligned, two lines, with a muted 15px subhead.
- [ ] A realistic, dense 12–13px product mockup sits directly under the hero, with a floating overlapping panel.
- [ ] Surfaces are #0f1011/#161718 with 1px low-alpha borders and 8/12px radii, and shadows are nearly absent.
- [ ] Feature sections use left heading plus right muted paragraph on a 12-col grid, with large edge-faded mockups.
- [ ] A mono "FIG" label and thin-line isometric SVGs appear in the three-column section.
- [ ] The only filled CTA is a light pill "Sign up". The header is 72px, fixed and blurred.
- [ ] Transitions are 0.1–0.16s, reveals are subtle, and the mobile layout crops the mockup instead of shrinking it.

You are building a premium fintech marketing homepage for **[PRODUCT]**, aimed at **[AUDIENCE]**, inspired by Stripe's homepage (not a clone: do not copy its logo, copy or imagery). The mode is persuade: a long, airy, confident landing page whose hierarchy comes from light-weight type, white space, one saturated accent and one signature gradient image. Fill the content from **[CONTENT]**.

### Tech stack
Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript. Plain CSS variables (below) with CSS Modules or Tailwind mapped to them. Fonts: Söhne Variable if licensed, otherwise Inter Variable via `next/font`, weight 300 and 400 only, plus Source Code Pro for code. Canvas or inline SVG for data visuals. IntersectionObserver for reveals. No animation libraries needed.

### Design tokens
```css
:root {
  --bg: #ffffff;
  --surface: #f8fafd;
  --wash: #e5edf5;
  --border: #e5edf5;
  --ink: #061b31;
  --ink-2: #50617a;
  --muted: #64748d;
  --accent: #533afd;
  --accent-dark: #362baa;
  --accent-tint: #d6d9fc;
  --success: #15be53;
  --dark: #0d1738;
  --on-dark-muted: #839bc8;

  --font-sans: "sohne-var", "Inter", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: "Source Code Pro", ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;

  --fs-h1: clamp(2.5rem, 3.4vw + 1rem, 3rem);   /* 48 */
